---------------------------------------------------------------------
TOM - To One Matching Compiler
---------------------------------------------------------------------


  What is it?
  -----------

  Tom is a pattern matching compiler, developed at Universite de Lorraine and
  Inria. It is particularly well-suited for programming various transformations
  on trees/terms.

  The Latest Version
  ------------------

  Details of the latest version can be found on the Tom Project
  web site <http://tom.loria.fr/>.

  The last 100% human-written version
  -----------------------------------

  The last commit written entirely by the human authors of Tom is
  2918e95c7, tagged v3-human-final; later commits were written with the
  help of an AI assistant (see README.md). To get that version:

    git clone git@github.com:rewriting/tom.git
    cd tom
    git switch -c human v3-human-final

  A frozen copy of it is also kept in legacy/ (see legacy/README.md).


  Documentation
  -------------

  The documentation is available at <http://tom.loria.fr>, in HTML 
  format

